ointed and much more efficient uses  gallons per  hour so making the switch from spray  irrigation to drip irrigation  from grass to plants and shrubs will  save you  55 gallons per square foot  think about this a square foot of grass  requires  10 feet of water every single year just  to survive  that's that's that's the depth of a  swimming pool that has a diving board  10 feet of water for a water smart  landscape  it only uses three feet of water so it's  a significant difference between grass  and drip irrigated trees and shrubs and  your landscape will  still look great it'll still look green  and it'll even bloom with flowers if you  select the red plants  starting in march you can increase your  watering  to three days a week those three days a  week  can be eased into you don't have to go  out and change it all at one time on  march first  instead wait until the weather tells you  it's time to change  when it gets hot when we get up into the  70s then you can go out there and slowly  increase your watering from one day to  two days  and then add that third day in the weeks  ahead  to learn more call the southern nevada  water water authority at 702-822-8543 or  visit  snwa.com and don't forget the  snwa's water smart landscapes rebate  program  provides cash incentives of three  dollars per square foot  for residents residences and businesses  to ditch grass  and upgrade to drip irrigated trees and  plants  las vegas now we'll be right back
 

